==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|yi|וויגריש}}, from {{der|en|ru|вы́игрыш||winnings}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|vigorishes}}

# {{context|uncountable|slang|lang=en}} A [[charge]] taken on [[bet]]s, as by a [[bookie]] or gambling establishment.
# {{context|uncountable|slang|lang=en}} The [[interest]] on a [[loan]] of money, especially for loans made by a [[usurer]] or [[loan shark]].
# {{context|countable|slang|lang=en}} An amount owed on account of or payment of a bookie's charge or of interest.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|charge on bets}} [[overround]], [[rake]], [[house take]], [[house cut]], [[house advantage]], [[vig]]
* {{sense|loan interest}} [[vig]], [[rake off]], [[cut]]

